    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0403" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg329"/>

                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 132.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 27, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Enclosed I transmit to you a few more
                    testimonials of sympathy received at this legation on the occasion of the
                    assassination of our late President. They are divided into three categories,
                    similar to those already transmit-fed by me with despatch No. 109, and numbered
                    in continuation of that series.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>[For enlosures see Appendix, separate volume.]</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d429-a1.xml" xpointer="d429-a1"/>
            </div>
